---
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import BackgroundEffects from "../layouts/BackgroundEffects.astro";
import "../styles/global.css";
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <title>IoT Mouse Trap</title>
  </head>

  <body class="bg-transparent text-white md:pl-24">
    <BackgroundEffects />
    <Header />

    <main>
      <!-- HERO -->
      <section
        class="relative overflow-hidden pt-40 pb-24 px-6 sm:px-10 md:px-16 lg:px-24"
      >
        <!-- glow background -->
        <div class="absolute inset-0 -z-10">
          <div
            class="absolute top-24 left-24 h-[28rem] w-[28rem] rounded-full blur-3xl animate-glow-slow"
            style="background: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.12)"
          >
          </div>
          <div
            class="absolute bottom-0 right-10 h-[30rem] w-[30rem] rounded-full blur-3xl animate-glow-slow"
            style="background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05)"
          >
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto">
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-12 gap-10 items-center">
            <!-- LEFT -->
            <div class="md:col-span-7">
              <span
                class="font-medium tracking-widest uppercase text-xs"
                style="color: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.8)"
              >
                Personal Project • 2023
              </span>

              <h1 class="mt-6 text-5xl md:text-7xl font-bold leading-[1.05]">
                Raspberry Pi <br /> Mouse Trap
              </h1>

              <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
                A smart IoT mousetrap system powered by a Raspberry Pi that
                detects movement using sensors and automatically triggers a
                mechanical capture mechanism. The goal was to explore embedded
                systems, automation, and sensor-based decision making.
              </p>

              <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 mt-10">
                {
                  [
                    "Python",
                    "IoT",
                    "Raspberry Pi",
                    "Sensors",
                    "Automation",
                  ].map((t) => (
                    <span class="px-4 py-2 rounded-full border border-white/10 bg-white/5 text-sm text-white/70">
                      {t}
                    </span>
                  ))
                }
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- RIGHT -->
            <div class="md:col-span-5">
              <div
                class="rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-white/10 bg-white/5"
              >
                <img
                  src="/images/Iot_Mouse_Trap.jpg"
                  alt="IoT Mouse Trap system diagram"
                  class="w-full h-full object-cover"
                />
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- VIDEO -->
      <section class="px-6 sm:px-10 md:px-16 lg:px-24 pb-24">
        <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto">
          <h2 class="text-4xl font-bold">System Demo</h2>
          <div class="w-16 h-[2px] mt-4 bg-[rgba(245,158,11,0.6)] rounded-full">
          </div>

          <p class="mt-6 text-white/50 max-w-2xl">
            The demo shows the full detection cycle: sensor input → Raspberry Pi
            processing → trigger activation of the mechanical trap system.
          </p>

          <div
            class="mt-10 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-white/10 bg-white/5"
          >
            <video
              class="w-full"
              autoplay
              muted
              loop
              playsinline
              preload="metadata"
            >
              <source src="/videos/Mouse_Trap_Demo.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
            </video>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <!-- PROJECT -->
      <section class="px-6 sm:px-10 md:px-16 lg:px-24 pb-32">
        <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
          <h2 class="text-4xl font-bold">Project</h2>
          <div class="w-16 h-[2px] mt-4 bg-[rgba(245,158,11,0.6)] rounded-full">
          </div>

          <div class="mt-12 space-y-10 text-white/70 leading-relaxed">
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">Context</h3>
              <p class="mt-3">
                This project was developed as part of the IoT Essentials course
                in the Bachelor of Applied Computer Science at Campus Geel. The
                goal was to design and implement a fully working Internet of
                Things system that combines hardware, sensors, and cloud
                communication into a functional prototype.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">
                Project — Smart Mouse Trap
              </h3>
              <p class="mt-3">
                The system is an automated mouse trap built around a Raspberry
                Pi. It detects movement using an ultrasonic echo sensor and
                triggers a mechanical capture mechanism when an object is
                detected within range. The trap includes a motor-driven door
                system, visual feedback through an LCD screen, and status
                indication via an LED and relay module.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">
                Hardware Components
              </h3>
              <p class="mt-3">
                The prototype integrates several hardware modules: a Raspberry
                Pi as the main controller, an ultrasonic distance sensor for
                detection, a stepper motor for the trap mechanism, an LCD
                display for system status, a relay board for electrical control,
                and physical buttons for triggering and resetting the system.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">
                Software Implementation
              </h3>
              <p class="mt-3">
                The software is written in Python and uses GPIO control via
                WiringPi. The system continuously measures distance readings,
                evaluates trigger conditions, and executes motor sequences when
                a target is detected. It also manages system states (armed /
                triggered / reset) and updates the LCD display in real time.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">IoT Integration</h3>
              <p class="mt-3">
                The trap is connected to the Ubeac IoT platform, where sensor
                data such as trap status and trigger count are uploaded in JSON
                format. This allows remote monitoring of system activity and
                historical tracking of trap events.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white">Outcome</h3>
              <p class="mt-3">
                The final result is a fully working IoT prototype that brings
                together sensors, real-time hardware control, and cloud
                connectivity. It combines embedded programming, mechanical
                design, and data communication into a single, functional smart
                system.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>
